# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

START get_item

    SET item to the item the player wants to collect
    SET current_room to the player's current room 
    SET inventory to the player's current inventory 

    OUTPUT "Enter the name of the item you want to get"
    INPUT item 
IF item is in inventory 
    OUTPUT "That item is already in your inventory"
ELSE     
    IF  item is in current_room
         ADD item to inventory 
         OUTPUT item + "added to inventory"
    ELSE
         OUTPUT "That item is not available in this room"
    END IF
END IF              


    
RETURN inventory

END get_item


